<p><strong>Postmark:</strong> A circular German cancel, mostly covering the stamp. The town name is only partly legible, but the visible letters are consistent with HOSTENBACH, the village pictured on the front. The date line is obscured; the final digits may read "14," but that reading is not secure. "3–4 N." below it is the collection hour (3 to 4 in the afternoon, <em>Nachmittag</em>).</p>

<p><strong>Stamp:</strong> 10 pfennig, Germania design, inscribed DEUTSCHES REICH.</p>

<p><strong>Addressed to:</strong><br>
An<br>
Mrs. Lizzie Zang<br>
Zangs Hotel<br>
Creede Box 466<br>
Colorado<br>
Nord Amerika</p>

<p><strong>Message</strong> (written sideways in pencil, in old German script; a working reading, since the pencil is faded and several letters are uncertain):</p>
<blockquote>Herzliche Grüße aus unserem neuen Heim senden Dir Michel nebst Frau und Kinder.</blockquote>

<p><strong>Translation:</strong></p>
<blockquote>Warm greetings from our new home, from Michel, with wife and children.</blockquote>

<p><strong>Printed on the address side:</strong> "175516 S. Reinartz, Völklingen," the publisher's number and name. Völklingen is a few miles from Hostenbach.</p>

